.TH ZIM-TO-MARKDOWN 1 "2026-11-09" "zim-to-markdown @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zim-to-markdown \- convert between Zim wiki pages and Markdown
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zim-to-markdown
[\fB\-\-direction\fR \fIDIRECTION\fR]
[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-images\fR \fIMODE\fR]
[\fB\-\-formatting\fR \fIMODE\fR]
\fIINPUT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zim-to-markdown
converts a single Zim page or a whole notebook to Markdown, and converts
Markdown back to Zim. A notebook is a directory or a path to its
\fInotebook.zim\fR file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-direction " " \fIDIRECTION\fR
\fBzim-to-markdown\fR (default) or \fBmarkdown-to-zim\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Output file for a single page; output directory for a notebook.
.TP
.BR \-\-images " " \fIMODE\fR
External images: \fBcopy\fR (default), \fBsymlink\fR or \fBrelative\fR;
notebook conversion only.
.TP
.BR \-\-formatting " " \fIMODE\fR
Inline formatting without a Markdown counterpart: \fBhtml\fR (default),
\fBbold\fR, \fBitalic\fR or \fBstrike\fR; Zim to Markdown only.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the application version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The process exits with 0 on success and with a non-zero status when the
arguments are invalid or when an input or output operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation at
\fIhttps://github.com/Tralen/zim-to-markdown\fR.
